WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.917
The two strands point in opposite directions. Follow the end labels: the template

00:00:04.917 --> 00:00:09.833
runs three prime to five prime. Its complementary strand runs five prime to

00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:14.750
three prime. These are different strands.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:19.778
Watch the complementary strand get longer. Each added nucleotide joins its three prime

00:00:19.778 --> 00:00:24.806
end. The five prime end stays at the start. Adding to the three

00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:29.833
prime end makes synthesis proceed five prime to three prime.

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:34.667
Keep these two descriptions together: DNA grows five prime to three prime, and

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:39.500
new nucleotides are added at the three prime end. Reading the template in

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.333
the opposite direction does not reverse new DNA synthesis.
